    "title": "UPDATE: Details released in Moline garage fire - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mike Colón Brian Weckerly ,\n20 hours ago\nUPDATE: A news release from the Moline Fire Department has more details on last night’s garage fire.\nThe Moline Fire Department responded to a report of a structure fire in the 4700 block of 26th Avenue on October 7 at about 10:14 p.m. The first crew arrived on the scene within five minutes and found a small, one-story unattached garage that was fully engulfed in flames. The home’s residents reported the fire and self-evacuated.\nThe fire was an immediate threat to the home and one nearby due to its intensity. Firefighters began an aggressive attack and brought the fire under control in about 20 minutes. Two vehicles parked in the driveway were involved in the fire and were damaged. Other crews ensured the fire did not spread in the homes.\nThe homeowners were not displaced as a result of the fire. The East Moline Fire Department, Rock Island Arsenal Fire Department, Rock Island Fire Department and MidAmerican Energy provided assistance at the scene. The cause of the fire is under investigation by the Moline Fire Department’s Bureau of Investigations. Anyone with information regarding the fire is asked to contact Fire Marshal Cunningham at 309-524-2250.\nEARLIER: A garage in Moline was severely damaged by a fire Tuesday evening.\nThe fire reportedly started around 10:15 p.m. in a garage behind a home in the 4700 block of 26th Ave.\nCrews from the Moline Fire Department, Moline Police Department and MidAmerican Energy were on scene battling the blaze.\nThe cause of the fire remains under investigation.\nThis is a developing story. Stay tuned to Local 4, Fox 18 and OurQuadCities.com for updates. Got a news tip? Forward it to Our Quad Cities News on Twitter or Facebook or download our app on your iPhone or Android phone.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHBF - OurQuadCities.com.\n1",
